messages.reasoning_content:
needsInput false until consumed all. Good. So large data test can work: after first inflate 8192, compressed retained. copy and return 8192. Next call compressed nonnull skip read, conditions false, inflate again. Eventually third call produces remainder and needsInput true closes compressed. Return 3616. Then next call EOF. Should work. Add large payload test to exercise loop and internal buffer refills. Use original 20000 repeated x; destination small or large. Need test result all bytes. `readFully` with dst allocate 4096 expected 20000, max uses:
1 4096 (copy 4096 from uncompressed, uncompressed remains 4096)
2 4096 (drain remaining, set uncompressed null)
3 next call inflater 8192 returns 4096 (uncompressed remains)
... etc. It should eventually. Could use destination 6000. This is a strong state test.

But if using `readFully` stops once exact original length; no EOF. Fine. Add.

What about incompressible data >8192 produces compressed also >8192. Our fake source chunk may be larger than compressed destination capacity. Its read handles splitting and requeues. Target `compressed` buffer 8192; gets first chunk. Inflates partial, if needsInput true closes compressed, returns some. Next call allocate, fake reads next compressed. This tests splitting. Multi-chunk currently compressed tiny and manually splits in 7 bytes. Large incompressible may be more representative. But our fake splits anyway. Could add only one broader test.

Potential issue byte pool size 8192 and original 20000 compresses tiny. Good.

Now maybe test `readFooter` branch through subclass? We can create a subclass:
```
class RecordingConduit extends InflatingStreamSourceConduit {
 int headerCalls, footerCalls, dataCalls...
 @Override protected boolean readHeader(ByteBuffer b) {// perhaps consume? return true}
 @Override protected void readFooter(ByteBuffer b) { footerCalls++; }
 @Override protected void dataDeflated(...) { ...}
}
```
But `readHeader` in target default true. If false, headerDone remains false and every new compressed chunk calls readHeader again. Not contract.
Could assert hooks called as observable side effect. But is subclass methods part target? They are callback. Maybe useful:
- dataDeflated called with output.
- readFooter maybe on finished.
However task target function only; side effects callbacks are part.
But adding callbacks tests may be overcomplicate. Current assertions reflect main behavior.

