```java
private long doWrite(ByteBuffer[] srcs, int offset, int length) throws IOException {
    if (failure != null) { writeInvocations++; throw failure; }
    writeInvocations++;
    long budget = Math.min(bytesPerWrite, zeroAfterTotalBytes - totalWritten);
    if (budget <= 0) { zeroWriteInvocations++; return 0; }
    long written = 0;
    for (int i = offset; i < offset + length && written < budget; i++) {
        ByteBuffer src = srcs[i];
        int toWrite = (int) Math.min(src.remaining(), budget - written);
        if (toWrite > 0) {
            byte[] tmp = new byte[toWrite];
            src.get(tmp);
            writtenOut.write(tmp, 0, toWrite);
            written += toWrite;
        }
    }
    totalWritten += written;
    return written;
}
```
Careful: iteration must continue to next buffer even if written < budget. Loop condition `i < end && written < budget` handles it.

